-- 613 La Trobe University
UPDATE scholarships SET
  title = 'La Trobe High Achiever Scholarship',
  description = 'La Trobe turns the weighted average mark directly into a discount, and the conversion table is published. A WAM of 60 to 74.9 earns the La Trobe High Achiever Scholarship at 20% off annual tuition, a WAM of 75 or above earns 25%, and the discount runs for the duration of the course as an upfront reduction applied from the first semester. There is no application: eligible international applicants are assessed automatically when the admission application is reviewed and the scholarship appears in the offer. The published window is 10 February 2026 to 31 December 2027, which covers the 2026 and 2027 intakes. The conditions that actually exclude people are worth stating plainly: you must be a citizen of a country other than Australia or New Zealand, a full fee-paying non-sponsored student, enrolling in a course on the eligible list, and not a humanitarian or other permanent visa holder. At the Sydney campus the discount starts from the second semester rather than the first. A separate Early Acceptance Grant pays A$2 000 once for accepting an offer early, and it can be stacked with the High Achiever discount - for a Semester 1 2027 start the offer has to be accepted by 22 February 2027.',
  requirements = 'Be a citizen of a country other than Australia or New Zealand and be a new international student commencing an undergraduate or postgraduate coursework program in a 2026 or 2027 intake. Be a full fee-paying, non-sponsored student. Apply to a program on La Trobe list of eligible courses. Hold a WAM of at least 60 for the 20% level, or at least 75 for the 25% level. Not be a humanitarian entrant or other permanent visa holder. No separate scholarship application is required: La Trobe assesses eligibility automatically with the admission application and states the outcome in the offer. To add the A$2 000 Early Acceptance Grant, accept the offer by the intake deadline, for example 22 February 2027 for a Semester 1 2027 start.',
  coverage_type = 'Partial Tuition', award_basis = 'variable', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = 'AUD', award_period = 'year',
  degree_levels = '["Bachelor''s","Master''s"]', eligible_majors = '["All Majors"]', eligible_countries = '["All"]',
  funding_type = 'Merit-based tuition fee reduction',
  tuition_coverage = '20% off annual tuition for a WAM of 60 to 74.9, 25% off for a WAM of 75 or above, applied for the duration of the course. At the Sydney campus the discount begins in the second semester. No living allowance.',
  english_requirements = 'The scholarship sets no separate English score; the La Trobe admission English requirement for the chosen course applies.',
  required_documents = '["La Trobe admission application","Academic transcripts used to calculate the WAM","English proficiency evidence","Offer acceptance and reduced deposit to confirm the scholarship"]',
  deadline = '31 December 2027 (the published closing date covering the 2026 and 2027 intakes); the Early Acceptance Grant for a Semester 1 2027 start closes on 22 February 2027',
  deadline_date = '2027-12-31', deadline_type = 'fixed', application_status = 'open',
  website_url = 'https://www.latrobe.edu.au/study/scholarships/other/la-trobe-high-achiever-scholarship',
  source_url = 'https://www.latrobe.edu.au/study/scholarships/other/la-trobe-high-achiever-scholarship',
  application_url = 'https://www.latrobe.edu.au/international/applying/scholarships',
  verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, amount_usd_value = 0,
  last_updated_at = now(), last_verified_at = now(),
  notes = 'Rewritten from the La Trobe University High Achiever Scholarship page fetched 2026-10-25 through the official search result for latrobe.edu.au/study/scholarships/other/la-trobe-high-achiever-scholarship, which gives the amount as up to a 25% reduction in course fees, the opening date 10 February 2026, the closing date 31 December 2027, the WAM table of 60 to 74.9 for 20% and 75 or above for 25%, the eligibility conditions including citizenship outside Australia and New Zealand, full fee-paying non-sponsored status, the eligible course list and the exclusion of humanitarian and other permanent visa holders, and the statement that the discount is applied from the first semester at Victorian campuses and from the second semester at Sydney. The La Trobe international scholarships page adds that the award is automatically assessed when applying, and the Early Acceptance Grant page gives the A$2 000 one-off value and the 22 February 2027 acceptance deadline for a Semester 1 2027 start. CORRECTIONS: the row was titled La Trobe International Scholarship, claimed a Partial Tuition award worth USD 27 000, listed all three degree levels and gave a variable October-November deadline. The real award is the High Achiever Scholarship at 20% or 25% of tuition, it is undergraduate and postgraduate coursework only, it needs no application, and the only published dates are an opening date and a 31 December 2027 close. amount_usd_value is 0 because La Trobe prices the award as a percentage.'
WHERE id = 613;

-- 619 Macquarie University
UPDATE scholarships SET
  title = 'Macquarie University Vice-Chancellor International Scholarship',
  description = 'The record named a pathway award that has moved; the flagship international award at Macquarie is the Vice-Chancellor International Scholarship, worth up to AUD 10 000 as a one-off reduction against tuition, and it is open year round. It applies to students commencing an undergraduate or postgraduate coursework degree, and the academic bar is a minimum ATAR equivalent of 85 for an undergraduate applicant or a WAM equivalent of 65 for a postgraduate applicant. The mechanics matter more than the number here: Macquarie does not consider you until you hold a full offer, and then you complete a short scholarship application form. It is explicitly a very limited award, which is why the university tells applicants to accept the offer and the scholarship early. It is a one-off payment against tuition, not a renewable discount, and it does not touch living costs, the student visa application, Overseas Student Health Cover, airfares or accommodation. Students who have any other Macquarie scholarship are excluded, and so are applicants already enrolled at or applying through Macquarie University College - the college runs its own smaller pathway awards instead, which is why the old title of this record no longer matches the flagship.',
  requirements = 'Be an international student commencing a Macquarie University bachelor or postgraduate coursework degree, excluding graduate certificates. Achieve a minimum ATAR equivalent of 85 for an undergraduate application or a minimum WAM equivalent of 65 for a postgraduate application. Hold a full offer of admission, since a scholarship application cannot be assessed before that, then complete the short scholarship application form. Commence in the session stated in the scholarship letter of offer. Not hold any other Macquarie University scholarship, and not be applying through or currently enrolled at Macquarie University College.',
  coverage_type = 'Partial Tuition', award_basis = 'variable', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = 'AUD', award_period = 'one_time',
  degree_levels = '["Bachelor''s","Master''s"]', eligible_majors = '["All Majors"]', eligible_countries = '["All"]',
  funding_type = 'Merit-based tuition fee reduction',
  tuition_coverage = 'Up to AUD 10 000 applied once against tuition. It is a one-off award, not renewable, and it covers no living costs, visa costs, health cover, airfare or accommodation.',
  english_requirements = 'The scholarship sets no separate English score; the academic and English entry requirements for the Macquarie degree apply.',
  required_documents = '["Full offer of admission to a Macquarie coursework degree","Scholarship application form","Academic transcripts showing the ATAR or WAM equivalent","English proficiency evidence","Passport copy"]',
  deadline = 'Applications are open year round; the award is confirmed in the scholarship letter of offer and is very limited, so early acceptance is advised',
  deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'rolling', application_status = 'open',
  website_url = 'https://www.mq.edu.au/study/admissions-and-entry/scholarships/international/vice-chancellor-s-international-scholarship/',
  source_url = 'https://www.mq.edu.au/study/admissions-and-entry/scholarships/international/vice-chancellor-s-international-scholarship/',
  application_url = 'https://it-mqu.formstack.com/forms/international_scholarship_applcation_form',
  verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, amount_usd_value = 0,
  last_updated_at = now(), last_verified_at = now(),
  notes = 'Rewritten from the Macquarie University Vice-Chancellor International Scholarship page fetched 2026-10-25, which states that applications close open year round, that the award value is up to AUD 10 000 as a fee reduction for a one-off award, that it is available to undergraduate and postgraduate international students, that it is highly competitive and very limited, that eligibility requires a minimum WAM equivalent of 65 for postgraduate applications or a minimum ATAR equivalent of 85 for undergraduate applications, that Macquarie University College pathway programs and Study Abroad may be considered only case by case, and that applicants must first receive a full offer and then complete a short scholarship application form. CORRECTIONS: the row was titled Macquarie University International College Scholarship, claimed a Partial Tuition award worth USD 28 000, listed all three degree levels and gave a variable October-December deadline. The College award is a smaller pathway scholarship that the university has described at AUD 3 000 and earlier at up to AUD 5 000, and its page could not be retrieved on 2026-10-25; the flagship award that an applicant from Uzbekistan should actually look at is the Vice-Chancellor International Scholarship at up to AUD 10 000, verified above. The old USD 28 000 figure matches nothing on the site. amount_usd_value is 0 although the provider publishes an AUD cap, because the award is a one-off credit rather than an annual value and mixing the two would misprice the record.'
WHERE id = 619;

-- 660 Queensland University of Technology
UPDATE scholarships SET
  title = 'QUT International Merit Scholarship',
  description = 'QUT pays a quarter of the tuition for as long as the results hold. The International Merit Scholarship covers 25% of tuition fees per semester of study, is awarded automatically when you apply for an eligible course, and continues for the duration provided the ongoing academic conditions are met; for courses in the Faculty of Health the 25% covers the first two semesters only. There is no separate form - QUT assesses the qualifications submitted with the course application and puts the outcome in the admission offer - and the academic threshold is published per country and per qualification rather than as a single global number: an Australian ATAR of 90, an IB admissions score of 34 studied in Australia, a completed Australian bachelor at GPA 5.0 on a 7-point scale for postgraduate entry, and a country-specific result for overseas qualifications. Grading systems not in the table are assessed at the time of application. Two exclusions are worth knowing before you plan around it: a student holding another QUT academic scholarship is not eligible, and the award does not stack. QUT also awards a College Merit Scholarship at the same 25% for the first semester of a diploma or foundation program, which is the pathway version of this award.',
  requirements = 'Be an international applicant for an eligible QUT undergraduate or postgraduate coursework program and be commencing the course for the first time. Meet the academic entry requirements for the course and the published country-and-qualification threshold for the scholarship, for example an Australian ATAR of 90, an IB admissions score of 34 studied in Australia, or a completed Australian bachelor at GPA 5.0 on a 7-point scale for postgraduate entry. Meet the minimum English language entry requirements, or complete a QUT pathway program first and become eligible once the degree starts. Not hold another QUT academic scholarship. No separate scholarship application is filed: QUT assesses the documents submitted with the course application and states the outcome in the offer.',
  coverage_type = 'Partial Tuition', award_basis = 'variable', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = 'AUD', award_period = 'year',
  degree_levels = '["Bachelor''s","Master''s"]', eligible_majors = '["All Majors"]', eligible_countries = '["All"]',
  funding_type = 'Merit-based tuition fee reduction',
